{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RemoteChange","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every field describes the whole burst, not its last notification. A burst is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one window as far as the merge is concerned, and “the last one wins” would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"silently drop every notification but one — on a debounce that exists","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"precisely because bursts are expected, that is a change quietly going","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"missing rather than a visible failure.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Only notifications the observer ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"accepted"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" are represented. A notification","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from a store the observer was told it doesn’t own is dropped before it gets","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"here; one whose store can’t be identified is always accepted, and sets"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/RemoteChange\/includesUnidentifiedStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Why there is no history token","level":2,"anchor":"Why-there-is-no-history-token"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The underlying notification carries "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPersistentHistoryTokenKey"},{"type":"text","text":", and it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deliberately not surfaced. That value is a CoreData "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPersistentHistoryToken"},{"type":"text","text":";"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the watermark in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" is a SwiftData "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DefaultHistoryToken"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose only public initializer is ","type":"text"},{"code":"init(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — there is no supported"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conversion between the two, and SwiftData’s interface names no CoreData type"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at all. Publishing a token that neither Swidux nor an app author can act on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"would be an invitation to misuse it.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing is lost by leaving it out: "},{"code":"PersistenceCoordinator.mergeChanges(into:policy:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anchors its watermark on the highest token in the window it just scanned, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the token it needs is one it already holds."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync"]]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/RemoteChange","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxcloudkitsync\/remotechange"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/RemoteChange\/init(storeURLs:storeUUIDs:includesUnidentifiedStore:notificationCount:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swid